  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Why Caching Exists & Where Caches Live",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cache, Defined",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A cache stores a response so a later equivalent request is served without a full origin round-trip. Every cached byte is a bet that the origin has not changed."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Latency win: no RTT to the origin",
            "Bandwidth win: the bytes never cross the wire",
            "Origin win: no compute, no DB hit",
            "Always a correctness / performance trade"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Private vs Shared",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Private",
                "lines": [
                  "Browser HTTP cache",
                  "Per-user, per-profile",
                  "Disk and memory",
                  "One person's bytes"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Shared",
                "lines": [
                  "CDN edge PoP",
                  "nginx / Varnish proxy",
                  "Corporate forward proxy",
                  "Serves many users"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Hierarchy On One Request",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "memory cache",
              "disk cache",
              "SW Cache API",
              "CDN edge",
              "origin shield",
              "origin"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Cache Key",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Default key = method + full URL",
            "Scheme, host, path and query all count",
            "`?v=2` is a different resource entirely",
            "`Vary` folds request headers into the key (ch 6)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Safe methods cacheable by default: `GET`, `HEAD`",
            "`POST` cacheable only with explicit freshness — rare",
            "Never assume a `PUT` response is stored"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Errors Cache Too",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Status",
            "Kind"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "200, 203, 204",
              "normal bodies"
            ],
            [
              "206",
              "partial content"
            ],
            [
              "300, 301, 308",
              "redirects"
            ],
            [
              "404, 405, 410",
              "client errors"
            ],
            [
              "414, 501",
              "also cacheable"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Heuristic Freshness",
          "items": [
            "No `Cache-Control`, no `Expires` = cache may guess",
            "Common guess: 10% of (`Date` − `Last-Modified`)",
            "You never chose that TTL and cannot see it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "Cache-Control: max-age=0, s-maxage=600",
            "Age: 500          # 500s spent at the edge",
            "# browser always asks, CDN absorbs 10 min",
            "# fresh for s-maxage - Age = 100s more"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Cache-Control: Lifetime, Scope & Revalidation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "No headers is not opting out",
          "text": "Shipping zero cache headers does not mean 'not cached'. It means cached by a heuristic you do not control."
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Fresh or stale — what changes?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Fresh: inside its lifetime, reused without asking",
            "Stale: past lifetime, must revalidate first",
            "Or be explicitly allowed to serve stale (ch 5)",
            "Stale is not invalid — only unverified"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Control Surface",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Cache-Control` is the modern surface; everything else is legacy",
            "Response directives are comma-separated",
            "Order-insensitive — no directive outranks by position",
            "Unknown directives are ignored, not rejected"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Lifetime Directives",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Directive",
            "Who obeys",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`max-age=N`",
              "all caches",
              "fresh N s after generation"
            ],
            [
              "`s-maxage=N`",
              "shared only",
              "overrides `max-age` at CDN"
            ],
            [
              "`Expires`",
              "all caches",
              "HTTP/1.0 date, loses to `max-age`"
            ],
            [
              "`Age`",
              "set by shared",
              "seconds already sat in cache"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Lifetime counts from `Date`, not from your arrival",
            "`Age` = seconds sitting in shared caches",
            "Remaining freshness = `max-age` − `Age`",
            "A CDN hit can land already 500s old"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Storage Scope",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`public` — shared caches may store, even with `Authorization`",
            "`private` — only the browser may store it",
            "`private` fits per-user HTML and dashboards",
            "`no-store` — never written to memory or disk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Revalidation Family",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`no-cache` lies by name: it stores, then revalidates every reuse",
            "`must-revalidate` — once stale, never served unchecked",
            "`must-revalidate` kills stale-on-error fallbacks",
            "`proxy-revalidate` — same, binding on shared caches only"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Precedence in one line",
          "text": "==s-maxage== beats `max-age` at the CDN, `max-age` beats `Expires` everywhere."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Legacy Headers, Freshness Math & Picking Directives",
      "blocks": [
        {
