    {
      "page_title": "Validators: ETag vs Last-Modified",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Read The Three Correctly",
          "items": [
            "`max-age=0` — stored, stale at once",
            "`no-cache` — stored, always revalidated",
            "`no-store` — never written anywhere"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Three defaults to memorise",
          "text": "`no-store` for secrets. `no-cache` for HTML. `max-age=31536000, immutable` for hashed assets."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What A Validator Is",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A validator is a token the client sends back so the origin can answer 'unchanged' cheaply. No body, no re-serialization, no render."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "ETag",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "ETag: \"a4f2c9\"        # strong: exact bytes",
            "ETag: W/\"a4f2c9\"      # weak: same meaning",
            "Last-Modified: Tue, 01 Sep 2026 10:00:00 GMT"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Opaque server-chosen version tag, quoted string",
            "Contents meaningless to the client — never parse it",
            "Strong `\"abc\"` = byte-for-byte identical",
            "Strong is required for `Range` and safe reassembly",
            "Weak `W/\"abc\"` = semantically equal, bytes may differ"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "What Makes A Tag Weak",
          "items": [
            "Whitespace or formatting churn",
            "A regenerated timestamp comment",
            "A different gzip compression level"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Last-Modified",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An `<HTTP-date>` with 1-second resolution",
            "Sub-second edits are invisible to it",
            "Breaks on deploy or `rsync` touching every file",
            "Breaks on content generated per request",
            "Breaks on clock skew across origin servers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Picking One",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "ETag",
                "lines": [
                  "Precise to the byte",
                  "Survives a `touch`",
                  "Costs CPU per request",
                  "Can differ per server"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Last-Modified",
                "lines": [
                  "Already known, free",
                  "1-second granularity",
                  "Consistent across a fleet",
                  "Lies after a deploy"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Send both when you can",
            "Clients echo both back on revalidation",
            "The origin picks the cheaper comparison"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Generating ETags Across a Fleet",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Generating ETags",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Strategy",
            "Verdict"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "content hash",
              "best"
            ],
            [
              "version + path",
              "good"
            ],
            [
              "mtime + size",
              "nginx default"
            ],
            [
              "`updated_at` + row id",
              "fine for APIs"
            ],
            [
              "inode",
              "never"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "nginx emits `ETag: \"mtime-hex-size-hex\"`",
            "Apache `FileETag INode` is the classic footgun",
            "Same file, different tag per box, zero hit rate",
            "gzip and brotli bodies need distinct strong ETags"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Fleet-Safe Config",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "apache",
          "lines": [
            "# Apache: drop the inode",
            "FileETag MTime Size",
            "# nginx: on by default",
            "etag on;"
          ],
          "note": "mtime must match across boxes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Deploy with preserved mtimes (`rsync -t`)",
            "Or hash at build and serve a stored ETag",
            "Test: `curl -I` each backend, tags must match"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Compression Changes Bytes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Body",
            "ETag"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "identity",
              "`\"a4f2\"`"
            ],
            [
              "gzip",
              "`\"a4f2-gz\"`"
            ],
            [
              "brotli",
              "`\"a4f2-br\"`"
            ],
            [
              "any, lazy option",
              "`W/\"a4f2\"`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Validator Lifecycle",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "origin sets ETag",
              "cache stores",
              "entry stale",
              "client echoes tag",
              "304 or 200"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Inode ETags behind a load balancer",
            "One strong tag shared by gzip and br bodies",
            "Hashing the full body on every request"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Precision vs consistency",
          "text": "ETag wins on ==precision==. Last-Modified wins on fleet consistency when ETags are inode-derived."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Conditional Requests & 304 Not Modified",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Hash at build time",
          "text": "Computing a content-hash ETag per request can cost more than just sending the body. Hash once at build or write time and store it."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When Stale Hits",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A stale entry is not thrown away. The cache revalidates — it asks whether its stored copy still stands, instead of refetching blind."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Conditional Headers",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`If-None-Match: \"a4f2c9\"` echoes the stored ETag",
            "That is the primary conditional header",
            "`If-Modified-Since` is used only when no ETag exists",
            "Both sent? Origin MUST use `If-None-Match`, ignore the date"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "GET /app.css HTTP/1.1",
            "If-None-Match: \"a4f2c9\"",
            "--> 304 Not Modified   # ~200 bytes on wire",
            "--> Cache-Control: max-age=60  # clock resets"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Two Answers",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Response",
            "Body",
            "Cache does"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "304",
              "empty",
              "refresh headers, restart TTL"
            ],
            [
              "200",
              "full",
              "replace entry wholesale"
            ],
            [
              "412",
              "empty",
              "write rejected"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "A 304 must carry fresh headers",
          "text": "Send an updated `Cache-Control`, `ETag` and `Date` on the 304. Forget them and the entry re-stales instantly, revalidating on every single hit."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Strong vs Weak Compare",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Strong compare: byte-identical, required for `Range`",
            "Weak compare: what `If-None-Match` uses on `GET`",
            "A `W/` tag can never satisfy a strong compare"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Write-Side Twins",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`If-Match` / `If-Unmodified-Since` guard `PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`",
            "Optimistic concurrency: send back the ETag you read",
            "`412 Precondition Failed` = someone else wrote first",
            "That is how a REST API avoids lost updates"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "It saves bytes, not time",
          "text": "A 304 still costs a full round trip. Revalidation buys bandwidth only — which is exactly why `immutable` assets matter."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Testing Revalidation with curl",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Test with curl, not reload",
          "text": "`curl -sI -H 'If-None-Match: \"a4f2c9\"' URL` — expect `304` and a refreshed `Cache-Control`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Lost Updates, Reloads & Round-Trip Costs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "If-Match: *         # must already exist",
            "If-None-Match: *    # PUT = create only if absent",
            "PUT /doc/7          # 412 if the ETag moved"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "What Your Reload Sends",
          "items": [
            "Normal reload: `Cache-Control: max-age=0`",
            "Ctrl+Shift+R: `Cache-Control: no-cache`",
            "The hard reload bypasses what you are testing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Lost Update, Prevented",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "GET /doc/7  -> ETag: \"v5\"",
            "PUT /doc/7",
            "If-Match: \"v5\"",
            "--> 412   # B saved \"v6\" first"
          ],
          "note": "re-GET, merge, retry the PUT"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Round Trip Costs",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Outcome",
            "Wire",
            "Latency"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "fresh hit",
              "0 bytes",
              "0 RTT"
            ],
            [
              "304",
              "~200 bytes",
              "1 RTT"
            ],
            [
              "200",
              "full body",
              "1 RTT+"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Stale Serving: SWR, stale-if-error, Collapsing",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "stale-while-revalidate",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`stale-while-revalidate=N` — serve stale now, refresh behind",
            "Background refresh allowed up to N s past expiry",
            "Removes revalidation latency from the critical path",
            "Cost: a bounded window of slightly old content"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "Cache-Control: max-age=60,",
            "  stale-while-revalidate=300",
            "# one user pays the miss",
            "# everyone else gets an instant hit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "stale-if-error",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`stale-if-error=N` — origin 5xx or timeout, keep serving stale",
            "Turns an origin outage into old content, not a 502 wall",
            "`must-revalidate` disables both stale behaviours",
            "Never pair it with `stale-if-error` and expect a fallback"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "entry expires",
              "request arrives",
              "serve stale",
              "refresh in bg",
              "entry fresh"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Collapsing",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "N concurrent misses for one key become 1 origin request",
            "Called coalescing at some CDNs, same mechanism",
            "Only works when the cache key matches exactly"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stampede",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Dogpile: a hot key expires and thousands of requests hit the origin in the same instant. The cache did not fail — it synchronised the failure."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Defence",
            "How it helps"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "collapsing",
              "N misses become 1"
            ],
            [
              "SWR",
              "miss never blocks"
            ],
            [
              "jittered TTL",
              "expiry spread out"
            ],
            [
              "early recompute",
              "refresh before expiry"
            ],
            [
              "origin shield",
              "one tier absorbs"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "import random",
            "max_age = 3600 + random.randrange(0, 601)",
            "# 3600..4200s, so a mass-filled cache",
            "# does not expire in lockstep"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Negative Caching",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cache 404s and 5xx briefly — 5 to 30 seconds",
            "A broken path then cannot hammer the origin",
            "Caching a 500 during a deploy pins the error in place",
            "Keep negative TTLs tiny for exactly that reason"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Same Ideas In nginx",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "nginx",
          "lines": [
            "proxy_cache_lock on;   # collapse",
            "proxy_cache_use_stale error",
            "  timeout updating;",
            "proxy_cache_background_update on;"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Staleness is a product call",
          "text": "Agree per route how old is acceptable. Engineering picks the mechanism, the product picks the window."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Vary: Cache Keys & Cardinality Traps",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Vary Extends The Key",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Vary` lists request headers folded into the cache key",
            "`Vary: Accept-Encoding` is the near-universal default",
            "Each distinct header value stores a separate variant",
            "Cardinality multiplies across every listed header"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "Vary: Accept-Encoding",
            "# gzip body and br body stay separate entries",
            "# omit it: br body sent to a gzip-only client"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "The corrupted page",
          "text": "Without `Vary: Accept-Encoding` a brotli body can be handed to a client that only accepts gzip. It cannot decode it and the page is garbage."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cardinality Killers",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Vary on",
            "Variants",
            "Verdict"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Accept-Encoding`",
              "2–3",
              "correct"
            ],
            [
              "`Accept-Language`",
              "normalize first",
              "fine"
            ],
            [
              "`User-Agent`",
              "thousands",
              "catastrophe"
            ],
            [
              "`Cookie`",
              "one per session",
              "use `private`"
            ],
            [
              "`*`",
              "never reusable",
              "full opt-out"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Vary: User-Agent` is roughly one variant per visitor",
            "`Vary: Cookie` is one variant per session ID",
            "`Vary: *` means never reusable, by anyone",
            "Both usually meant `private` instead"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Legitimate Uses",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Vary: Accept-Language`, normalized to `en`, `fr`, `de`",
            "`Vary: Origin` when you reflect `Origin` into CORS",
            "Skip it and you leak CORS grants across sites"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "CORS Needs Vary: Origin",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "Access-Control-Allow-Origin:",
            "  https://a.example",
            "Vary: Origin",
            "# no Vary: site B reuses A's grant"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Cookie? Reach For private",
          "items": [
            "`Vary: Cookie` shards the CDN per session",
            "`private` keeps it in the browser only",
            "Same safety, no wasted edge storage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Language, Normalized",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Raw header",
            "Key"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`en-US,en;q=0.9`",
              "en"
            ],
            [
              "`fr-CA`",
              "fr"
            ],
            [
              "`de-DE,de`",
              "de"
            ],
            [
              "`ja`",
              "en (fallback)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Map to a small fixed set at the edge",
            "Rewrite the header before it hits the key",
            "Every unmapped value falls back to one default"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Normalizing Vary at the Edge",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Every Vary is a multiplier",
          "text": "Only list headers that ==actually change the body==, and only after normalizing them."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "# edge: normalize before keying",
            "if \"br\" in ae:     enc = \"br\"",
            "elif \"gzip\" in ae: enc = \"gzip\"",
            "else:              enc = \"none\""
          ],
          "note": "3 variants instead of hundreds"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Normalize At The Edge",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Collapse `Accept-Encoding` to `gzip` | `br` | `none`",
            "Then `Vary` on the normalized value only",
            "Most CDNs let you define the cache key directly",
            "Key on device class, country, or one named cookie"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Or Skip Vary Entirely",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Vary",
                "lines": [
                  "One URL",
                  "Variant per header value",
                  "Hit rate splits",
                  "Debuggable only at edge"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Distinct URLs",
                "lines": [
                  "`/hero.avif`",
                  "`/hero.jpg`",
                  "No `Vary` needed",
                  "Perfect hit rate"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Why is Vary multiplicative?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Key = URL × each listed header's value",
            "2 encodings × 3 languages = 6 stored copies",
            "Add `User-Agent` and it is 6 × thousands"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Hit Rate Mysteriously ~0%?",
          "items": [
            "Print the response `Vary` header first",
            "Count the distinct values it can produce",
            "One stray `Vary: Cookie` explains most cases"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
